{"id": "d616168e-aba2-49ee-9ba6-7210391dc515", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:18:03.828061", "source": "user", "parent_id": "832d8312-bc5b-49c9-a31a-59a068675871", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task: I need a benchmark experiment design (no execution) comparing JaxMARL's MPE Simple Spread against the original CPU-based MPE from PettingZoo on steps-per-second under random actions. For this first step, do ONLY the following and report back:\\n\\n1. Input/repository inspection: Look at /workspace (and any docs you can reach offline) to see what is actually available — JaxMARL version, whether the MPE Simple Spread environment exists there, the PettingZoo MPE counterpart, and any existing benchmarking scripts or README guidance. Report concrete findings, not assumptions.\\n\\n2. Proposed approach (brief): How you would measure steps-per-second fairly on both sides — e.g., environment step (and reset) timing under uniformly random actions, warm-up vs steady-state measurement, batched/vectorized stepping on the JAX side, number of repeated runs, and which hardware you would pin each implementation to. Keep this a sketch, not the full design.\\n\\n3. Assumptions and uncertainties: List anything consequential you are assuming — e.g., matching environment configurations (same number of agents/landmarks, observation and action spaces, episode length), whether JAX should run with or without JIT tracing/warm-up effects, how vectorized envs count toward \\\"steps-per-second\\\", CPU/GPU availability, and any setup detail not covered by the known context (JaxMARL is JAX-based/GPU-accelerated; baseline is PettingZoo MPE).\\n\\nDo NOT produce the final experiment design or run anything yet. Just inspection findings, a proposed direction, and your key assumptions so I can review the approach before authorizing the main work.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the performance of JaxMARL in the MPE Simple Spread environment compare to its original CPU-based counterpart in terms of steps-per-second under random actions?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_5\", \"neurips2024/97649/2:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
