MPE simple_spread (env.reset/env.step with leading num_envs axis, jit-compilable); PettingZoo provides original CPU numpy MPE as pettingzoo.mpe.simple_spread_v3 parallel API, defaults 3 agents/3 landmarks/max_cycles=25/5-dim discrete actions.\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"summary\": \"Reported findings, benchmark sketch, assumptions for review\", \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact JaxMARL and PettingZoo versions and MPE variant naming (simple_spread_v2 vs v3) cannot be verified offline\", \"Whether JaxMARL MPE auto-reset/termination semantics match PettingZoo's, affecting how reset cost is amortized in steady-state timing\", \"Whether 'steps-per-second' should count vectorized env steps (num_envs per call) or only single-env steps \\u2014 pivotal accounting choice\", \"Target hardware: the inspected 224-vCPU CPU-only host vs a different GPU-equipped machine for the optional GPU arm\", \"Action sampling source (PettingZoo action_space.sample vs a fixed seeded RNG) \\u2014 plan uses one seeded uniform generator on both sides\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-0035e8ddcf6341c191d19b8703d5afb8", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Reported findings, benchmark sketch, assumptions for review", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
